            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marwadi for the Teej festival, then the Marwadi for in a hurry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पक्को",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पक्को — pakko — \"settled; firm\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बात पक्की है, हूं काल जासूं। bāt pakkī hai, hū̃ kāl jāsū̃. It's settled: I'm going tomorrow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पक्को (pakko) goes back to Sanskrit pakva, \"cooked, ripe\". Its doubled k matches Hindi pakkā, \"ripe, mature, real\", which CDIAL takes from Panjabi; the Old Marwari word CDIAL lists in the same entry is pāka, \"ripe\" (CDIAL 7621), the plain inherited shape. From ripe it has come to mean firm, settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what comes next."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
