              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "टालणो (ṭālṇo) is inherited from Sanskrit ṭalati, \"moves aside\", through its causative ṭālayati; CDIAL lists Marwari ṭālṇo, \"to pass (time)\", and Hindi and Gujarati verbs for averting and avoiding under it (CDIAL 5450). To move a plan aside is to put it off."
